  "body": "Stacked on #2001 (merge #2001 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nKeep oversized numeric controls aligned to the start of their allocated space.\nThe tool editor keeps its width across 100 frames with the pointer moving.\nThe fix changes `fields::num_sized` and preserves its width budgets and unit conversion.\nThe issue commit changes no tool editor column widths.\nRecord the decision in `docs/decisions/2003-tool-editor-width.md`.\nEffort: low.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe feed-rate `DragValue` exceeds the shared 96-point field budget when it draws `1800.0 mm/min`.\nThe old `ui.add_sized` centers the oversized control.\nIts leading edge overflows by 1.8125 points.\nThat overflow feeds the next window layout and adds 1.8125 points per frame.\nThe existing tool editor grew from 770 to 951.25 points over 100 pointer frames.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll four pins pass in the default UI value-test suite.\n\n- `existing_tool_editor_width_stays_put_after_100_pointer_frames` failed before the fix.\n- `new_tool_editor_width_stays_put_after_100_pointer_frames` covers the new-tool path and passes on both versions.\n- `wide_metric_feed_tool_editor_width_stays_put_after_100_pointer_frames` covers a long metric feed.\n- `wide_inch_feed_tool_editor_width_stays_put_after_100_pointer_frames` covers a long inch feed.\n\nThe mutation check copied the actual `upstream/main` version of `fields.rs` back into the worktree.\nThe existing-tool and both long-feed pins failed at runtime.\nThe wide metric case grew from 770 to 1314.8125 points.\nThe wide inch case grew from 770 to 1305.1563 points.\nAll four pins passed after restoring the fix.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all four steps with zero failures.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe required gate also covers the inherited #2001 changes.\n\n## Tool editor before and after pointer movement\n\nThese are 1280 × 720 headless renders of the shipping egui shell, captured with the existing-tool width-test setup and its 100 pointer-movement frames. The viewport is the harness placeholder. They are review evidence, separate from snapshot goldens.\n\nThe before renders use the original `num_sized` implementation from this issue commit's parent. The editor grows from 770 to 951.25 points. The after renders use this PR's fixed implementation. Its width stays at 770 points.\n\n| Implementation | Initial frame | After 100 pointer frames |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before | ![Before: initial editor width 770 points](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/92400b9b58b87b08cfa9ba61d65ef63164d33d55/2020/before-initial.png) | ![Before: editor width grows to 951.25 points](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/92400b9b58b87b08cfa9ba61d65ef63164d33d55/2020/before-pointer100.png) |\n| After | ![After: initial editor width 770 points](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/92400b9b58b87b08cfa9ba61d65ef63164d33d55/2020/after-initial.png) | ![After: editor width stays at 770 points](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/92400b9b58b87b08cfa9ba61d65ef63164d33d55/2020/after-pointer100.png) |\n\nThe four PNGs are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch at `92400b9b58b87b08cfa9ba61d65ef63164d33d55`. Temporary capture code was removed. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe NC and CL golden diff against `upstream/main` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo manual native-window session or release-lane pixel snapshot was run.\nThe other floating dialogs received a source audit.\nThe machine editor, G-code viewer, post refusal, and Debug info windows specify default sizes or widths.\nThe fixture library and unsaved prompt cap their content widths.\nThe G-code viewer also bounds its trace columns.\nThe audit found no reason to change those dialogs in this issue.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2001 changes `tool_editor_window`, which was the expected edit site during the overlap check.\nThis branch starts at its head `028a0ad0e`.\nThe final fix lives in `fields::num_sized` instead.\n#2001 must merge first.\n\n#1931 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n#1717 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nBoth change WCS properties in `pages.rs`.\nThe `pages.rs` changes in this branch come unchanged from #2001.\nThe overlap check found no open PR touching `fields.rs` or `tests/tool_cutter.rs`.\n\nChangelog: Keep the tool editor width stable when numeric values exceed their field width.\n\nFixes #2003\n",
